{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289461-non-artifact-artifacts-and-evocations","id":1289461,"title":"Non-Artifact Artifacts and Evocations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-19T03:53:38-08:00","id":1289461,"title":"Non-Artifact Artifacts and Evocations","content":"Maybe more of a thought experiment/topic for discussion than anything else but what are people's thoughts on what makes an Artifact or allows for Evocations?<br /> I know it sounds like a stupid question, but really... does it need to be made of magical materials? Does it need to have been an Artifact when crafted or could it become one over time? Are Evocations dependent on the magical nature of an Artifact to be able to be expressed or could a sufficiently storied or legendary item have the ability to have some anyway?<br /> <br /> Let's say you have a regular sword, not made of orichalcum or moonsilver or jade, but of steel, it's not the most amazing sword ever, but it is well crafted. It's a families heirloom sword, now wielded proudly by a brave Solar swordsman, it carries his family legacy. It was granted to his great grandfather when he was ennobled after the great battle of the Golden Plains, it was in his grandfathers hands when he cut down the arch-traitor Koteshin, it still has the notch in the blade where it caught on the war-collar of the horrifying demon-beast H'Kul when his father lost his life and now it is in the hands of a man beginning to carve a legend for himself that has the potential to shake the very pillars of Creation. <br /> This swordsman is not going to give this blade up for any other, no matter how shiny or magical or better it's stats might be because this blade is storied and connected to him in a real, fundamental way that no weapon of the First Age could compete with.<br /> But it's just a sword, an ordinary sword.<br /> <br /> It just feels to me that there is more joy to be had in allowing items like this to develop evocations that in a fancy jade axe he could grab from a random Dynast he fights, even if it is a storied axe with a legend of it's own, it isn't his legend.<br /> And what if we say after using his faithful blade for many years his essence suffused strikes have bled some of his very Exalted nature into the wood and steel and it becomes almost unbreakable, or even gains the stats of a daiklaive? Is that okay? Is it in keeping with the feel of Exalted or is it nonsense? Can mundane materials ever be more than just mundane?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T04:34:38-08:00","id":1289468,"title":"","content":"I think the idea is supposed to be that magical materials (and it doesn't need to be <i>the</i> magical materials, just something sufficiently mystical) are required to hold the power and the magic that evocations provide. A exalt who has a favourite mundane sword would just have charms representing what they did with it.<br /> <br /> But now you've got me thinking of a regular sword that gets Grandfather's axe'd into a daiklave. Like first the blade breaks, so it's reforged with orichlacum, and then the handle wears away and is replaced by jade, and then the crossguard is strengthened with moonsilver...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T06:03:03-08:00","id":1289484,"title":"","content":"I've mused on the idea of updating Path of the Arbiter Style and having it able to nominate a sentimental item to become the style's form weapon and awaken evocations from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289461-non-artifact-artifacts-and-evocations?p=1289468#post1289468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But now you've got me thinking of a regular sword that gets Grandfather's axe'd into a daiklave. Like first the blade breaks, so it's reforged with orichlacum, and then the handle wears away and is replaced by jade, and then the crossguard is strengthened with moonsilver...</div> </div> </div> </div> Or if you want to keep more of the original sword around, it could have a kintsugi effect going on with veins of orichalcum running through the steel.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T07:37:20-08:00","id":1289522,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, the reason weapons in Exalted do more damage is because they're huge. The magic is what lets you wield them like they were normal weapons instead of sharpened bulldozer blades. As such, it is difficult to imagine an entirely mundane sword turning into an artifact.<br /> <br /> That said, you can theoretically tie a Sorcerous Working to an object, and ...I dunno. Having a legacy item that's been passed down for generations (repaired as necessary) with potential for at least one ghost haunting it... That feels like something magical and unique but I'm not sure that mundane metal can withstand or take advantage of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T08:34:15-08:00","id":1289538,"title":"","content":"Something that could work, especially since your hypothetical is of a Solar swordsman, is that the heirloom blade gets augmented by Glorious Solar Saber, which instead of summoning a blade, temporarily awakens the true potential of the history within your family's sword. Glorious Solar Saber allows for Evocations to be built from it, and drawing from the history of the blade and your family would certainly be a consistent theme for those Evocations.<br /> <br /> In the hands of anybody but the Solar, it's just a really old blade, but the Solar is able to realize its true potential and draw it forth; at least to me, that seems like it would hit the major thematic notes that you seem to be aiming for.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T09:34:23-08:00","id":1289563,"title":"","content":"There's a Solar Charm to let you get some limited Evocations about something meaningful like an ancestral weapon, although for the most part that power requires a commensurate investment of resources and expertise.<br /> <br /> Hmm, am I able to post as normal again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-19T10:03:35-08:00","id":1289570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289461-non-artifact-artifacts-and-evocations?p=1289538#post1289538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that could work, especially since your hypothetical is of a Solar swordsman, is that the heirloom blade gets augmented by Glorious Solar Saber,</div> </div> </div> </div>This is definitely how I'd do it, yeah. You could even re-fluff Glorious Solar Saber's summonability as meaning that your heirloom weapon is instantly reformed, good as new, even if something breaks it.<br /> <br /> For other types of Exalted, I'd look at their own weapon-enhancing charms. Dragon-Blooded have Dragon-Graced Weapon, for example - I think an Essence 3 charm chaining off that and making a single mundane but cherished weapon into an artifact, and letting you buy evocations for it, sounds fine. We don't know the whole Lunar charmset yet, and don't know if they have any equivalents, but I believe they did in 2e, so it wouldn't surprise me to see that return, in which case I'd build off that for them. And this whole idea of &quot;a mundane item gains magical powers because of its connection to you&quot; seems almost perfectly tailored to Sidereals.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T06:09:32-08:00","id":1289887,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the commentary and suggestions, and should it ever matter then yes, I would likely go with the ideas about refluffing GSS as it's straightforward enough, can't really break anything as far as I can see, and already has all the rules hardcoded.<br /> <br /> But, fundamentally, I think the reason I posted this was because I struggle to see what the restrictions about what is and isn't an artifact and such really add to the game or the themes of Exalted, it feels more ideal that an items power can increase with it's legend, and a legendary item shouldn't be entirely reliant on the materials used in it's construction. Frankly I blame Qin for doing such a nice job of modelling how the fame of a great hero can make their weapon more than simply a weapon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T06:53:39-08:00","id":1289904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289461-non-artifact-artifacts-and-evocations?p=1289563#post1289563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a Solar Charm to let you get some limited Evocations about something meaningful like an ancestral weapon, although for the most part that power requires a commensurate investment of resources and expertise.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is? What charm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T08:10:21-08:00","id":1289930,"title":"","content":"Legend-Spirit Convocation from Miracles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T09:04:07-08:00","id":1289958,"title":"","content":"Ah, the Lore charm. I can see why they went with that, but I'm not sure that unleashing the legendary power of the (non-daiklaive) sword of kings should require you to be one of the greatest polymaths and scholars in Creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> <br /> So I rarely take Exalted artefact weapons. They just feel too... ludicrous. I can't take Final Fantasy weapons seriously, except in a magitech-and-anime game.<br /> <br /> But I guess you can say, like &quot;My daiklaive is the size of a bastard sword&quot; and generally use it two-handed, one-handed occasionally (let's be honest, most PCs with a Daiklaive don't have a weapon in the other hand anyway).<br /> I have taken a single Short Daiklaive before and used it as a longsword.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, the materials.<br /> In some ways, I do like the idea that a smith forges a weapon of incredibly sharpness and strength from certain materials.<br /> Meteoric steel.<br /> Pure silver.<br /> The souls of the dead bound into the metal, giving it the strength of the dead.<br /> Jade, for Wuxia.<br /> Metal forged in a volcano.<br /> <br /> But for some of those, the associates mythologically are rather off. Silver is associated with purity; killing beasts and demons. Not madness and dreams. Meteoric steel is associated with incredible strength, rather than spirits and bizarre fate-bending. Forging a weapon in a volcano should give it fire-powers, not sunlight or holy powers.<br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> I think that... I don't know, they're a bit overused? Like, if a quarter of artefact weapons' thing is they're &quot;made from Jade&quot;, that's kind of dull. What's more interesting is the other stuff; made from the tooth of a behemoth, woven from the skin of a dragon, etc, etc.<br /> Not to mention the fact so many are just found in a tomb or looted from a Dragonblood's corpse. (Obviously the writers have tried to improve that by putting in the whole evocation thing.)<br /> <br /> <br /> In the game I used to, players had a lot of artefact weapons.<br /> The fire-sorceress had a giant golden sword that she got from... somewhere? Before the game. Red jade would have fit her better. Or a demon sword, actually. (If Arms had been out, I think she'd have taken Soulfarer.) Also a couple of daiklaives looted from DBs.<br /> The Lunar had a silver blade and a soulsteel blade looted from enemies.<br /> The Zenith had a big golden staff.<br /> The Dawn had a golden blade.<br /> There was also a starmetal spear (looted from an enemy) and a couple more jade daiklaives sitting in people's huts, looted from DBs.<br /> Later, when I played, I made 2 blue jade short daiklaives from the blue jade fighting sticks I took from a Thunderbird I killed.<br /> <br /> (Oh, and only the Dawn had artefact armour. No-one else did. Which made the combats fast-paced, I guess.)<br /> <br /> Honestly, the only one I really liked was the Full Moon's staff, which was made from his own tusk and the soul of Chejop Kejak, who'd tried possessing him once.<br /> The rest were pretty dull. Including the ones I made.<br /> <br /> And yes, I'm sure someone's going to say &quot;Well, that's because they didn't have a cool story.&quot; And that's a little true. But after the first one, more golden blades are, let's be honest, kind of boring. &quot;Oh, it's another blade made of solid alchemy-gold. Whup-tee-do.&quot;<br /> <br /> I should say that Arms is mixed here; there are steel weapons that just have magical material inlay or whatever. And there's stuff like a giant tusk of a monster, or a stone prison with a demon eye in.<br /> But others are purely because of their legend, and not really what they're made of, and at that point, isn't Fodor right? It's just the legend afterall, not the material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T10:34:47-08:00","id":1290000,"title":"","content":"I've been mentally fitting the Evocation system to handle all sorts of situations.<br /> <br /> A family-heirloom would be an excellent example.<br /> <br /> Also, using it as the basis for a Charm tree for lesser-powered god-blooded, demon-blooded, and the like. Basically it's just a Charm tree that's not tied to any one particular Ability or Attribute, and can customize its costs and conditions.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T11:00:11-08:00","id":1290015,"title":"","content":"In my games, Artifacts are only slightly larger and heavier than their mundane counterparts (if a mortal sword is 3 feet long and weighs 3 lbs, a Daiklave would be 3 1/2 feet and weigh 6 lbs), meaning they can be used by mortals with a penalty, or as a weapon one Size category higher without penalty.<br /> <br /> ive never been a fan of the fuckhuge-weapons of Vanilla Exalted. Artifacts deal the damage they do because they are *magical*, not because they are large enough to use as an ironing-board.<br /> <br /> I also allow mortals to make their own Artifacts, so long as they spend a suitable amount of XP and do suitably-kickass things with the thing beforehand. A mortal killing something large and gribbley *means something*, and if they do choose part of their legend enters their weapon as a result.<br /> <br /> For example, in one of my Quests the mortal fought and killed an Anathemic Lunar in a corrupted shrine to Luna. He resanctifed the shrine by sacrificing his broken spear, and as a gift Luna sent dreams to his boss suggesting she commission a replacement weapon for him. No Magical Materials involved, just skilled mortal artifice, feathersteel and silver, but it was ended up being a fairly powerful Direlance (which he would have discovered if the Quest actually finished :/)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T08:32:11-08:00","id":1290361,"title":"","content":"0 0<br /> __<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2026..<br /> <br /> It is unfair and unreasonable to be so angry at a post that happens to express a very different opinion of something that you so dearly love in the game. You wish to be a fair and reasonable man. Hence, you shall endeavour to keep it in check.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289461-non-artifact-artifacts-and-evocations?p=1289958#post1289958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But others are purely because of their legend, and not really what they're made of</div> </div> </div> </div>No they're not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T08:40:36-08:00","id":1290366,"title":"","content":"Why not? What thematic resonance does a big gold sword have that makes it worthy of magic powers that a small steel sword doesn't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T08:42:20-08:00","id":1290370,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm sure mortals weapons are a lot more similar to artifacts if you change literally everything about the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T09:02:11-08:00","id":1290380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289461-non-artifact-artifacts-and-evocations?p=1290361#post1290361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No they're not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realise, upon re-reading my last sentence, that... I actually don't understand what I meant. It may be a typo, it may not, I can't remember. So I can't really defend that.<br /> <br /> The rest of it I'm sticking to unless someone comes up with an interesting counterpoint, but I'm not sure what I meant there. Sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-21-2019, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T10:03:54-08:00","id":1290410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289461-non-artifact-artifacts-and-evocations?p=1290380#post1290380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The rest of it I'm sticking to unless someone comes up with an interesting counterpoint</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that I or anybody else can argue against how you feel, it's just very very different from how I feel, and I was obnoxiously trying to have my cake and eat it to by making a big public gesture of reminding myself to keep perspective, thus still alluding to having an issue.<br /> <br /> I am invested in Artifacts as they currently are on three personal fronts. I have an enjoyment of technical and production matters such that I've always been sold on the image that the setting has made about the intricate background to the creation of magical items since the earliest time that I heard it. I have always been dissatisfied by the realisation of magical items across fiction (despite the prior impulse, combined with a general admiration for tools, instruments and the products of human artifice, compelling me towards <i>wanting</i> to like them), which the basic concept and ultimate execution of Evocations finally addressed. And I have found the backstories of several Artifacts and the manner in which their powers evoke them to be deeply moving, in a way that I think is unique in the setting, and would diminish it were it absent.<br /> <br /> Pyre of Legions is eminent here; a sword imprinted with the noble last sacrifice of an otherwise disappointing Dynast, that allows those who wield it to emulate her sacrifice by burning themselves up for the defence of allies and opposition when outnumbered, but also carries the promise of hope for better prospects for the Dynast's successors by an ultimate power to make the sacrifice demanded of prior powers non-harmful to their bodies.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of that being a thing at the same time as I like the idea that making a device capable of carrying that thing was a matter of particular effort and expertise.<br /> <br /> I like the magical materials, because I just like the whole notion of knowing and using the properties of things. I have a book filled with literal poetry describing the properties and applications of the properties of the elements of the periodic table, that I keep on my bedside table. It is a constant delight to me.<br /> <br /> Hell, an attachment to an idea of magical materials, something close to <i>these</i> magical materials, was cultivated in me from before I ever had anything to do with Exalted. Mage the Awakening had things like that as well, right down to orichalcum and moonsilver (the rest were all things unified by alchemical significance). They were disappointing; apparently Second Edition is going to do something better with them.<br /> <br /> Oh, Golden Sun, I really loved what the second game there did with the descriptions and little icons given to all kinds of quirky raw materials that you could dig up, and some of the really neat magical weapons and armour that you could get made out of those. Heck, that even had a kind of star metal very similar in theme to the Exalted one. And Golden Sun is one of my favourite games ever.<br /> <br /> Hmm, now I want to go back and look at wiki descriptions of all of the gear you could have forged in Golden Sun...<br /> <br /> Again, my point here is to give background for why I feel as I do, not convince people that do not share it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T10:13:41-08:00","id":1290413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1289461-non-artifact-artifacts-and-evocations?p=1290410#post1290410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the magical materials, because I just like the whole notion of knowing and using the properties of things. I have a book filled with literal poetry describing the properties and applications of the properties of the elements of the periodic table, that I keep on my bedside table. It is a constant delight to me.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This explains so much about your point of view to me, that whole idea of knowing and understanding is something I get, but is anathema to me when it comes to a setting that, for me, is built on myth and legend and mystery of things beyond comprehension. What gives you joy in artifacts at the same time robs me of the magic and immersion I feel they should hold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25050-fodor","name":"FODOR","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T10:28:33-08:00","id":1290420,"title":"","content":"I feel the need to state that it's not a strict dichotomy, because even a lot of myth describes products of divine artifice as requiring particular rarefied raw materials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T10:28:47-08:00","id":1290421,"title":"","content":"I don't think either me or Fodor are arguing against the first point, of the legend. In fact, the supremacy and importance of the legend is I think exactly what he is arguing for, though I suppiose his point is that the magic comes after the legend of how it's used. (But I'll let him express that himself, in case I've misunderstood. I should probably explain for anyone who doesn't know, that Qin, which Fodor referenced, is a game in which at high levels you get Weapon XP or something, representing the legend of your blase, which itself improves the blade. So a mortal blade slowly becomes magical as its wielded by a hero. I don't know exactly how it works, as I never managed to have a Qin character who survived long enough to get lots of XP.)<br /> <br /> The second point, that forging a magical blade should be a matter of particular effort and expertise, I also agree with you; partly because of the thing itself, it's thematic weight, etc, but also because a game that features epic Crafters ought to have something that only they can add to the group.<br /> <br /> <br /> The materials... I don't hate them. They're just no longer exotic or exciting to me. If one PC has a blade of alchemical gold forged in a volcano, that's cool. When five party members have one, they're not.<br /> <br /> And that... yeah, I'll agree it's purely subjective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-21-2019, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}